    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but \"shaping a story\" assumes there's actually a choice to be made. if the blueprint is already flawed, if the neurochemistry is just destined to collapse like everyone else in my family did, then maybe the \"strength\" you're talking about is just an illusion. it feels more like accepting the truth. like, if the end is written, why keep struggling to change a script that can't be changed? wouldn't it be more honest to just... stop fighting the current?",
